---
title: "About"
description: "Lead Hardware Engineer — FPGA architectures, embedded systems."
---



I’m a hands‑on digital hardware engineer with experience across analogue circuits, high‑speed digital design, embedded systems, and FPGA development. My work spans biomedical, automotive, and satellite communication applications, where I’ve delivered practical, reliable solutions from concept to deployment.

I design and program embedded systems using PIC, AVR, ARM microcontrollers, and FPGAs from Xilinx and Intel. I also work extensively with Matlab, Python, C/C++, VHDL and Verilog for algorithm development, signal processing, simulation, and verification.

This site collects my projects, publications, and technical notes — a mix of research, engineering work, and practical examples.

